# --- added by T-001 (the six no-app-code gates) -----------------------------
# gitleaks and Trivy are NOT npm packages; they are static binaries installed
# into the toolbox image (docker/toolbox.Dockerfile, secops-fetch stage) with
# checksum verification against the publisher's signed SHA256SUMS.
#
# ONE THING TO KNOW BEFORE YOU BUMP EITHER LINE. scripts/dev is T-000's and
# T-001 does not modify it, so it passes only NODE/PNPM/TERRAFORM/PLAYWRIGHT
# as --build-arg and the image tag encodes only those three. Changing a
# version here therefore does NOT invalidate the cached image on its own.
# That hole is closed by `gate:toolbox`, which compares the running binaries
# against these lines and fails with "rebuild the toolbox" if they disagree.
# So: edit the line, then `scripts/dev --build <anything>`, then
# `scripts/dev pnpm gate:toolbox` to confirm. The Dockerfile's ARG defaults
# mirror these values and must be edited in the same commit.
gitleaks 8.30.1
trivy 0.74.0
